      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">In &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;, the gene &lt;i&gt;LUP1&lt;/i&gt; was heterogously expressed in a &lt;i&gt;Saccharomyces cerevisiae&lt;/i&gt; yeast mutant unable to cyclize oxidosqualene and therefore lacking background activity |CITS:[9883589],[10930257]|. This enzyme was shown to allow the formation of a variety of triterpene compounds including |FRAME:CPD-90| (39%), |FRAME:CPD-6951| (39%), |FRAME:CPD-6948| (8%), |FRAME:GERMANICOL| (7%), |FRAME:CPD-6949| (4%) and |FRAME:CPD-6950| (3%) |CITS:[10930257]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G78970-MONOMER" />
